  "evidence": "TEXT_E: Replace the Human Rights Act with a British Bill of Rights; strong immigration controls (net migration target, deport-first/appeal-later, English fluency for public-facing roles); maintain strong Armed Forces, renew the nuclear deterrent, uphold NATO; update communications powers and new tools against non-violent extremism; welfare cap, benefit freezes, lower household cap, Youth Allowance with work/training requirements; aim for budget surplus, raise Personal Allowance and higher-rate threshold, continued crackdown on tax avoidance. TEXT_G: Protect human rights law and oppose blanket surveillance; decriminalise drug possession and presume against short prison terms; reduce nuclear patrol posture; strong pro‑EU engagement; progressive tax measures (restrict non-dom, levy on £2m+ homes, bank tax); extensive green targets (net‑zero by 2050, end unabated coal by 2025, strict shale rules); significant NHS/mental health and carers support, Living Wage in central government.",
